# --- Model (consumed by DeepSeek Harness, not by this repo) ---
#
# The harness reads its credentials from the *launching environment*, so export
# this when you invoke `dsh`, e.g.
#
#   DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=$(grep -m1 '^DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=' .env | cut -d= -f2-) \
#     dsh --profile headless "<task>"
#
# Note that dsh refuses to boot when the *working directory* contains a .env that
# sets DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL, so run it from somewhere other than this repo.
#
# Do NOT add DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL or DEEPSEEK_MODEL here: that is exactly the
# anti-hijack fence described above.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here

# --- Browser ---
#
# Nothing browser-related belongs in this file any more. The browser is the
# third-party `dsh-browser` bundle, configured through the DSH profile, and it
# exposes no headless/recordVideo/slowMo keys at all — its launch options are
# hardcoded. A visible window is achieved by scripts/patch-dsh-browser-headed.mjs,
# controlled at run time with DSH_BROWSER_HEADED=0. See the README.
